 "about": [
  "<h2>About this page</h2>",
  "The sprinters are the Bolt sprinter model (NVIDIA Warp physics, 136 muscles) controlled by neural networks trained with reinforcement learning. The main test and the changed conditions come from this week's trained networks, the 23 Oct races from the runs of 22 Oct. Each network was run once in the simulator from the same start, and its bones and muscle paths were recorded 30 times per second.",
  "Practice: starting from one of 3 trained sprinters, every copy trained 20,000 more iterations. The twin trained without a device; the others with a hip device whose torque (up to 25 N·m per hip) is set by the sprinter's own network, on in half of the runs or in all of them, or with a resisting hip torque (a brake) in half of the runs.",
